<p>NOTE: (a)  The special charge of $48.9 million for the fiscal year ended March 28, 1997, relates to the Aug. 1, 1996 acquisition of The Continuum Co. Inc.  The charge, net of income taxes, is $35.3 million or 45 cents per share.  During last year's quarter ended Dec. 29, 1995, $26 million of purchased research and development was expensed in connection with the acquisition by Continuum of SOCS Holding.  The charge, which carried no tax deduction, is 34 cents per share.</p>
<p>During last year's fourth quarter, a special charge of $50.1 million was expensed in connection with Continuum's acquisition of Hogan Systems.  This charge, net of income taxes, is $35.7 million or 47 cents per share.  All fiscal 1996 amounts have been restated to reflect the Continuum acquisition, which was accounted for as a pooling of interests.</p>
